This is something I've been wondering about for some time now, but
could never remember to ask.

Why is it that shields and metallic armour interfere with
spellcasting?  When I first read the spoilers I assumed it was because
metal interferes with magic in the same way lead blocks x-rays. 
However, most people seem to be saying it's because one needs mobility
to properly cast spells and any armour that is hard to move in will
reduce your chance of success.  I suppose that explains why shields
interfere with spellcasting, but why do metallic helmets and boots do
the same?  I find myself going back to my "magical interference"
theory more and more.

Sooo...what *is* the explanation?  If it's mobility, shouldn't helmets
and boots be excluded?  Especially helmets, as I can't see any way for
them to interfere with movement *or* magic waves.  If magic
interference is the problem, then shouldn't magical metals (i.e.
mithril) be excluded?

Oh, and back to the mobility thing: if that's the case then shouldn't
crystal plate mail carry a penalty as well?  I can't picture *anyone*
moving around easily in that.  They should be just as bulky as regular
plate mail, if not more, no?

